This project of a Discord bot that presents due dates of upcoming assignments in our current class for the semester can
be implemented to all classes in the future with a few updates of the code and changing the token into one the professor has
so that way it can be steadily used. 

I think this can help students of Professor Bisestis as we are on discord more for class communication than we are on brightspace.
Many wonder when assignments are due and this chatbot can make it very simple to stay informed for each class.

I got the general code within a week of starting this assignment but spent a lot of time on 4/28 getting the bot setup for testing, and then 
had to manipulate little things in my code to get it to work. Mainly, getting my VSCode to read the right .env. I had many from writing other codes 
so I wrote the program to force read a certain pathway to the .env that had the discord token in it. 

This bot is similar to the haiku bot but different in a sense that you have to input a command to get a response and the program has the data loaded
into it instead of scraping websites to generate random poems. Once this bot is cleaned up and gets updated for each class it will be a great tool.
